cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these records or this code, please cite the repository as below."
title: "C4 recovery-regimes study: trial records, client and analysis"
abstract: >-
  Trial records, client, runner and analysis for a measurement study of what two
  self-hosted WebRTC selective forwarding units, LiveKit and Janus, report when a
  participant's session is disrupted and recovers, compared with receiver-defined audio
  recovery. 215 cited trials, 30 superseded trials, development runs and a follow-up
  measurement.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Nirmal
    given-names: Jay Suresh
repository-code: "https://github.com/jaynirmal15/c4-recovery-regimes"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - WebRTC
  - selective forwarding unit
  - session recovery
  - observability
  - measurement
